<h2 id="exercises-section-ass" class="tex-section"><span data-tag="0CR7">111.10</span> Associated primes</h2>

<p>
Associated primes are discussed in Algebra, Section <a href="/tag/00L9" data-tag="00L9">10.63</a> 
</p>
<p>
<article class="env-exercise" id="0CR8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CR8">Exercise <span data-tag="0CR8">111.10.1</span>.</a> Compute the set of associated primes for each of the following modules. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$R = k[x, y]$ and $M = R/(xy(x + y))$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$R = \mathbf{Z}[x]$ and $M = R/(300x + 75)$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$R = k[x, y, z]$ and $M = R/(x^3, x^2y, xz)$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Here as usual $k$ is a field. </p>
</article> 
</p>
<p>
<article class="env-exercise" id="0CR9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CR9">Exercise <span data-tag="0CR9">111.10.2</span>.</a> Give an example of a Noetherian ring $R$ and a prime ideal $\mathfrak p$ such that $\mathfrak p$ is not the only associated prime of $R/\mathfrak p^2$. </p>
</article> 
</p>
<p>
<article class="env-exercise" id="0CRA">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CRA">Exercise <span data-tag="0CRA">111.10.3</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a Noetherian ring with incomparable prime ideals $\mathfrak p$, $\mathfrak q$, i.e., $\mathfrak p \not\subset \mathfrak q$ and $\mathfrak q \not\subset \mathfrak p$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Show that for $N = R/(\mathfrak p \cap \mathfrak q)$ we have $\text{Ass}(N) = \{ \mathfrak p, \mathfrak q\} $. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Show by an example that the module $M = R/\mathfrak p \mathfrak q$ can have an associated prime not equal to $\mathfrak p$ or $\mathfrak q$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article> 
</p>
